From: Denys Vitali <denys@denv.it>
Subject: [PATCH] ARM: dts: omap4: espresso10: SMB347 HC mode, battery supplier

Select USB high-current mode at 1.8 A; the NV default (USB5, 500 mA) does
not cover the system load. On a wall charger 1.8 A nets about +0.75 A against
+0.4 A at 900 mA. It trips the over-current limit of a Raspberry Pi 4 host
port. Link the fuel gauge to the charger, so that the battery status is no
longer "Unknown".
---
--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/ti/omap/omap4-samsung-espresso10.dts	2026-11-17 06:59:11.869999899 +0000
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/ti/omap/omap4-samsung-espresso10.dts	2026-11-17 07:01:06.672504061 +0000
@@ -17,7 +17,21 @@
 			summit,enable-usb-charging;
 			summit,enable-charge-control = <SMB3XX_CHG_ENABLE_SW>;
 			summit,chip-temperature-threshold-celsius = <120>;
-			summit,usb-current-limit-microamp = <1800000>;
+			/*
+			 * HC mode as the vendor kernel uses for its charger.
+			 * Without it the chip stays in USB5 (500 mA), which
+			 * does not cover the system load. 1.8 A is for wall
+			 * chargers; it trips the over-current limit of some
+			 * USB host ports (seen on a Raspberry Pi 4).
+			 */
+			summit,usb-hc-mode;
+			summit,usb-current-limit-microamp = <1800000>;
+		};
+	};
+
+	i2c-gpio7 {
+		fuel-gauge@36 {
+			power-supplies = <&smb347>;
 		};
 	};
 
